## Function Process Generation

compile → send → parse → verify per card; a compile fault or stale inputs discard the answer; accepted cards fire the commit hook.

Behaviour: processGeneration(cards, deps, root) compiles every card with compileCard, keeping each card's input digest; sends all variants of all cards in ONE sendGeneration(deps.config, requests, deps.transport) call (so deps.config's concurrency pools across the whole generation) and slices answers and usage back to each card by request index; then verifies each card in input order. Per card: a compile fault → {status: "failed", reason "compile: <first fault message>", acceptanceLog = the fault messages joined by "
"}; else recompute the digest (captureInputs) and compareCaptures against the compile digest — a non-empty change → {status: "failed", reason "stale inputs", acceptanceLog "stale inputs: <changed paths, comma+space joined>"} and no acceptance is run; else build one VariantAnswer per variant (variant id "<customId>.v<n>"; a null-text answer becomes {corrupt: the answer's error ?? "no text returned"}, else parseAnswer(text, targets)) and call verifyCard with timeoutMs = deps.acceptanceTimeoutMs ?? DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS (300000, Run Acceptance's default) — the acceptance has its own timeout, never the processor's HTTP deps.config.timeoutMs. Accepted → {status: "written", winningVariant = the accepted variant id, acceptanceLog = the winner's log, earlierFailures = the logs of the rejected variants tried before it, commit = the sha from deps.commit(customId, targets), diffstat from the hook}; no variant accepted → {status: "failed", reason "acceptance failed", acceptanceLog = the last variant's log, earlierFailures = the earlier variants' logs, commit null, diffstat null}. attempts is 1 for every outcome of one round. Returns {outcomes, usage, requests, retryContexts}: usage is the Usage of every request sent; requests is one Request Usage per request sent, in send order ({customId: the request id, model: the request's model ?? deps.config.model, provider, generationId, inputTokens, outputTokens, cost from its Usage, finishReason and error from its Answer}); retryContexts holds one Retry Context per FAILED outcome, keyed by its customId, in outcome order, and nothing for a written card. A compile fault or stale inputs → {acceptanceOutput: the outcome's acceptanceLog, previousDiff: null}. A rejected card → of the variants whose acceptance ran (the verify result's diff is not null), the one that got FURTHEST gives {acceptanceOutput: its log, previousDiff: its diff, "" when the attempt changed nothing}: furthest = the greatest stageCount(log), a tie → the later variant; stageCount(log) (exported) is the number of lines of the log, split on "
", that begin with "== " (the stage headers the acceptance prints: == tsc, == probe, …). When no variant ran (every answer corrupt or truncated) → {acceptanceOutput: the last result's log, previousDiff: null}. The log and the diff of the retry always come from the same attempt, and previousDiff is null exactly when no acceptance ran. The outcome's acceptanceLog and earlierFailures do not change (the last variant's log, the earlier ones'). Every variant sent gets one Variant Record, given to deps.onVariant when it is set (optional; without it nothing changes), after its card is decided (an accepted card's commit hook first), in card order then variant order: {request: the Request as sent, text, finishReason, error (its Answer's), verdict, stages, lastStage}; verdict "stale" for every variant of a stale card, else "corrupt" or "truncated" by its parsed answer, else "untried" when Verify Card stopped before it, "accepted" for the winner, "rejected" otherwise. For accepted and rejected, stages = stageCount(its log) and lastStage(its log) (exported: the text after "== " of the log's last stage header, null when none); else 0 and null. A card with a compile fault sends nothing and gets no record.

